#### Decision Table Testing

Decision tables must be tested with a coverage matrix: at least one test per rule that confirms the action fires when all conditions are met, and at least one test per condition that confirms the rule does not fire when that condition is not met.

```csharp
// C# xUnit example
[Theory]
[InlineData("professional", "not-icd10", "REJECT")]
[InlineData("professional", "icd10", null)]      // no match expected
[InlineData("institutional", "not-icd10", "REJECT")]
public void ClaimValidationTable_DiagnosisFormatRule_FiresCorrectly(
    string claimType, string diagnosisCodeFormat, string? expectedOutcome)
{
    var table = ClaimValidationTableLoader.Load("claim-validation-v1.json");
    var evaluator = new DecisionTableEvaluator<ClaimContext, ValidationAction>(
        table, NullLogger.Instance);
    var context = new ClaimContext { ClaimType = claimType, DiagnosisCodeFormat = diagnosisCodeFormat };

    var actions = evaluator.Evaluate(context);

    if (expectedOutcome is null)
        Assert.Empty(actions);
    else
        Assert.Contains(actions, a => a.ReasonCode == expectedOutcome);
}
